    "optimization"
  ],
  "statement": "A wooden stick has length `L`. You must cut it at `k` marked positions `c_1 < c_2 < ... < c_k` (each strictly between `0` and `L`), in any order you like. Cutting a piece costs **the length of the piece you cut** (you cut one piece into two at a time, and every cut is made on the piece that currently contains the marked position). Find the minimum total cost to make all `k` cuts.\n\n**Input.** The first line holds `L` and `k`. The second line holds the `k` positions in increasing order (it may be empty when `k = 0`).\n\n**Output.** The minimum total cost.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ L ≤ 10^9",
    "0 ≤ k ≤ 1000 in this browser version (the Knuth speed-up lets the idea scale to about 5000)",
    "0 < c_1 < c_2 < ... < c_k < L"
  ],
  "timeLimitMs": 2000,
