  "hints": [
    "The first cut splits the stick in two independent sub-sticks, each with its own marked positions. That is an interval DP: dp[i][j] is the cheapest way to make all cuts strictly between points i and j. With all k choices for the first cut it costs O(k^3), too slow for k = 1000.",
    "dp[i][j] = min over m with i < m < j of dp[i][m] + dp[m][j], plus the length p[j] - p[i]. The added length is the same for every m, and its structure (it satisfies the quadrangle inequality) means the best m moves monotonically.",
    "Knuth's optimisation: let opt[i][j] be the best first cut. Then opt[i][j-1] <= opt[i][j] <= opt[i+1][j], so it is enough to try m between those two values. Summed over each diagonal of intervals the work is O(k), so the total is O(k^2)."
  ],
  "editorial": "Let `p_0 = 0, p_1..p_k` be the cut positions and `p_{k+1} = L`. Let `dp[i][j]` be the minimum cost of making every cut strictly between `p_i` and `p_j` on a piece that spans exactly from `p_i` to `p_j`. With no cut inside (`j = i + 1`) the cost is `0`. Otherwise some cut `m` is made first: it costs the length of the piece, `p_j - p_i`, and leaves two independent pieces, so `dp[i][j] = min over i < m < j of (dp[i][m] + dp[m][j]) + p_j - p_i`. Evaluating this directly is `O(k^3)`. The cost function `w(i, j) = p_j - p_i` satisfies the **quadrangle inequality** (`w(a, c) + w(b, d) <= w(a, d) + w(b, c)` for `a <= b <= c <= d`; here it holds with equality) and is monotone on the lattice of intervals, which implies **Knuth's monotonicity**: if `opt[i][j]` is the smallest minimising `m`, then `opt[i][j-1] <= opt[i][j] <= opt[i+1][j]`. So for each interval only the candidates between those two stored values need to be tried. For all intervals of a fixed length `gap` the ranges telescope: `opt[i][j]` is bounded by `opt[i+1][j]` and the next interval's lower bound is `opt[i+1][j]`, so the total number of candidates over one diagonal is `O(k)`, and over all `k` diagonals `O(k^2)`. Process intervals by increasing length, initialise `opt[i][i+1] = i`, and take care to use 64-bit arithmetic: the answer can reach about `L * log k` and more in adversarial shapes. The same optimisation applies to optimal binary search trees and to merging adjacent piles. Compare with the plain `O(k^3)` interval DP lesson: only the loop bounds of the innermost loop change.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n^2)",
    "space": "O(n^2)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "import sys\n\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\nlength, k = int(data[0]), int(data[1])\np = [0] + [int(x) for x in data[2:2 + k]] + [length]\n",
    "javascript": "const lines = [];\nlet line;\nwhile ((line = readLine()) !== null) lines.push(line);\nconst tok = lines.join(' ').split(/\\s+/).filter(s => s.length).map(Number);\nconst length = tok[0], k = tok[1];\n// the cut positions are tok[2 .. 2 + k - 1]\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long length = sc.nextLong();\n        int k = sc.nextInt();\n        // read k positions\n    }\n}\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    long long length;\n    int k;\n    scanf(\"%lld %d\", &length, &k);\n    // read k positions\n    return 0;\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "import sys\n\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\nlength, k = int(data[0]), int(data[1])\np = [0] + [int(x) for x in data[2:2 + k]] + [length]       # the cut points, including both ends of the stick\nsize = k + 2\ndp = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]                     # dp[i][j]: cheapest way to make all cuts strictly between p[i] and p[j]\nopt = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]                    # opt[i][j]: the cut chosen first in the best solution\nfor i in range(size - 1):\n    opt[i][i + 1] = i\nfor gap in range(2, size):\n    for i in range(size - gap):\n        j = i + gap\n        best, arg = None, -1\n        for m in range(max(opt[i][j - 1], i + 1), min(opt[i + 1][j], j - 1) + 1):   # Knuth: the best first cut lies between the neighbours' best cuts\n            v = dp[i][m] + dp[m][j]\n            if best is None or v < best:\n                best, arg = v, m\n        dp[i][j] = best + p[j] - p[i]                      # cutting a piece of length p[j] - p[i] costs its length\n        opt[i][j] = arg\nprint(dp[0][size - 1])\n",
    "javascript": "const lines = [];\nlet line;\nwhile ((line = readLine()) !== null) lines.push(line);\nconst tok = lines.join(' ').split(/\\s+/).filter(s => s.length).map(Number);\nconst length = tok[0], k = tok[1];\nconst p = [0];\nfor (let i = 0; i < k; i++) p.push(tok[2 + i]);\np.push(length);\nconst size = k + 2;\nconst dp = Array.from({ length: size }, () => new Float64Array(size));\nconst opt = Array.from({ length: size }, () => new Int32Array(size));\nfor (let i = 0; i + 1 < size; i++) opt[i][i + 1] = i;\nfor (let gap = 2; gap < size; gap++) {\n  for (let i = 0; i + gap < size; i++) {\n    const j = i + gap;\n    let best = Infinity, arg = -1;\n    for (let m = Math.max(opt[i][j - 1], i + 1); m <= Math.min(opt[i + 1][j], j - 1); m++) {\n      const v = dp[i][m] + dp[m][j];\n      if (v < best) { best = v; arg = m; }\n    }\n    dp[i][j] = best + p[j] - p[i];\n    opt[i][j] = arg;\n  }\n}\nconsole.log(String(dp[0][size - 1]));\n",
    "java": "import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        StreamTokenizer st = new StreamTokenizer(new BufferedInputStream(System.in));\n        st.nextToken();\n        long length = (long) st.nval;\n        st.nextToken();\n        int k = (int) st.nval;\n        long[] p = new long[k + 2];\n        for (int i = 1; i <= k; i++) {\n            st.nextToken();\n            p[i] = (long) st.nval;\n        }\n        p[k + 1] = length;\n        int size = k + 2;\n        long[][] dp = new long[size][size];\n        int[][] opt = new int[size][size];\n        for (int i = 0; i + 1 < size; i++) opt[i][i + 1] = i;\n        for (int gap = 2; gap < size; gap++) {\n            for (int i = 0; i + gap < size; i++) {\n                int j = i + gap;\n                long best = Long.MAX_VALUE;\n                int arg = -1;\n                for (int m = Math.max(opt[i][j - 1], i + 1); m <= Math.min(opt[i + 1][j], j - 1); m++) {\n                    long v = dp[i][m] + dp[m][j];\n                    if (v < best) { best = v; arg = m; }\n                }\n                dp[i][j] = best + p[j] - p[i];\n                opt[i][j] = arg;\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(dp[0][size - 1]);\n    }\n}\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\nint main() {\n    ll length;\n    int k;\n    scanf(\"%lld %d\", &length, &k);\n    vector<ll> p(k + 2, 0);\n    for (int i = 1; i <= k; i++) scanf(\"%lld\", &p[i]);\n    p[k + 1] = length;\n    int size = k + 2;\n    vector<vector<ll>> dp(size, vector<ll>(size, 0));\n    vector<vector<int>> opt(size, vector<int>(size, 0));\n    for (int i = 0; i + 1 < size; i++) opt[i][i + 1] = i;\n    for (int gap = 2; gap < size; gap++) {\n        for (int i = 0; i + gap < size; i++) {\n            int j = i + gap;\n            ll best = LLONG_MAX;\n            int arg = -1;\n            for (int m = Math.max(opt[i][j - 1], i + 1); m <= Math.min(opt[i + 1][j], j - 1); m++) {\n                ll v = dp[i][m] + dp[m][j];\n                if (v < best) { best = v; arg = m; }\n            }\n            dp[i][j] = best + p[j] - p[i];\n            opt[i][j] = arg;\n        }\n    }\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", dp[0][size - 1]);\n    return 0;\n}\n"
  }
